WEBVTT
NOTE Cedwyn film, frame 007, en. Timings are estimates from the script until the clip is rendered.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.154
<v Nia>Bore da. Two plans of Tŷ Mawr, about ten years apart, from two different family collections.

2
00:00:06.504 --> 00:00:08.304
<v The Grandson>These are printouts.

3
00:00:08.654 --> 00:00:14.423
<v Nia>Catalogue entries. We haven't seen either original plan yet. The request slips go in today.

4
00:00:14.773 --> 00:00:20.158
<v Nia>Glamorgan Archives, DMAT/279: 'Late 18th-century plan of Ty Mawr farm, Llandough, then Gedrych property.'

5
00:00:20.508 --> 00:00:25.123
<v The Grandson>Gedrych. Not a name I've met in any of the family papers.

6
00:00:25.473 --> 00:00:42.012
<v Nia>Nor me. It sits among the estate plans of the Mathew family of Radyr and Llandaff, dated about 1790. It shows the farm was worth drawing, and was filed with that family's estates. From the entry alone it doesn't show who farmed it.

7
00:00:42.362 --> 00:00:44.285
<v The Grandson>So no Williams on it.

8
00:00:44.635 --> 00:00:53.865
<v Nia>No tenants named in the entry at all. When the original comes up, we look for fields, buildings and any writing in the margins.

9
00:00:54.215 --> 00:00:59.985
<v The Grandson>DXJF/61/12. 'Plan of Ty Mawr farm, Llandough', circa 1800. Corbett Family of Cogan Pill Papers.

10
00:01:00.335 --> 00:01:04.950
<v The Grandson>A different family's papers. Did the farm change hands between the two?

11
00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:18.762
<v Nia>Maybe. Or one family kept a copy of another's plan; estates passed surveys around. Two catalogue lines can't tell us which. And 'circa' means the date was judged from the drawing, not written on it.

12
00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:23.727
<v The Grandson>Then it goes in as two plans, two collections, one open question.

13
00:01:24.077 --> 00:01:25.877
<v Nia>Ingredients, not a verdict.

14
00:01:26.227 --> 00:01:31.227
<v Nia>While surveyors paced those fields, the village was building. It's up the hill.

15
00:01:31.577 --> 00:01:35.038
<v The Grandson>Penlan Road, corner of Lewis Road. This is it?

16
00:01:35.388 --> 00:01:43.465
<v Nia>The former National School, built 1821. Coflein, the national monuments record, has it as site 31824, grid reference ST 16740 73140.

17
00:01:47.815 --> 00:01:50.892
<v The Grandson>Did Tŷ Mawr children learn their letters here?

18
00:01:51.242 --> 00:01:59.319
<v Nia>The record dates the building and puts it on the map. It doesn't list pupils. If registers survive, they're somewhere else.

19
00:01:59.669 --> 00:02:04.669
<v The Grandson>Thirty-one years: two drawings of the farm, and a schoolroom on the hill.

20
00:02:05.019 --> 00:02:10.404
<v Nia>Next, an 1824 surveyor who wrote the farm's name two ways. Bring a pencil.
